      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Read-through is 2 to 4 percent for all four positions \u2014 low, but not zero. Across three tandem units the compounded leak is enough to lift the OFF state of a gate by roughly 8 percent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Design rule adopted"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Transcription units are oriented divergently wherever the vector allows, so read-through terminates into a non-coding region rather than into the next unit."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
